# T-35: does the deepmd-bundle LAMMPS carry `compute sna/atom` (the
# ML-SNAP package)? A three-cell diamond-silicon box, no real potential
# (pair_style zero — only the neighbour list matters), one bispectrum
# compute at a FIRST-SHELL cutoff, dumped per atom. If the package is
# absent LAMMPS stops at the compute line with "Unrecognized compute
# style", which is the answer as much as a dump is.
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
lattice         diamond 5.43
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 28.0855
pair_style      zero 3.0
pair_coeff      * *
# The SNAP cutoff is rcutfac x (R_i + R_j): with rcutfac 1.0 and
# R_1 = 1.3 A the cutoff is 2.6 A — the first shell (2.35 A) in, the
# second (3.84 A) out — and it fits inside the 3 A neighbour list.
# (First submission used R_1 = 2.6 => 5.2 A and LAMMPS refused, which
# itself proved the ML-SNAP package is present.) twojmax 6 gives 30
# components per atom.
compute         sna all sna/atom 1.0 0.99363 6 1.3 1.0 rmin0 0.0
dump            d all custom 1 sna_check.dump id type x y z c_sna[*]
dump_modify     d sort id
run             0
